{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brunette-bellicose-blacklemur","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while running full `make test` as the local pre-flight for janitor leaf b35a. **Five** tests in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py` FAIL on a clean checkout of `origin/main` (reproduced in a throwaway worktree at origin/main, freshly `make install`ed), independent of any janitor change:\n\n- test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head\n- test_successful_push_followed_by_remote_rewrite_fails_closed\n- test_unrelated_remote_rejection_merges_and_rebuilds_private_candidate\n- test_lost_push_ack_is_confirmed_without_publishing_a_second_bundle\n- test_post_push_convergence_preserves_concurrent_local_delivery_pending\n\n## Evidence\n\nFailing assertion (representative):\n`assert _git(remote, \"rev-parse\", \"refs/heads/tickets\") == remote_tip` → `git -C <tmp>/tickets-remote.git rev-parse refs/heads/tickets` returns exit 128 (ref does not exist on the fixture bare remote).\n\nEnvironment: git **2.55.0** (very new), init.defaultBranch=main, user set. Fails both in isolation and in-module (5 failed, 12 passed). These are all remote push/rejection/rewrite semantics for the tickets branch.\n\n## Hypothesis to investigate (RCA required, do not fix blind)\n\nCI keeps origin/main green, so either (a) these tests are environment/git-version-sensitive (git 2.55.0 changed push-rejection or default-ref behavior such that the fixture remote never ends up with refs/heads/tickets), or (b) a genuine latent breakage CI doesn't exercise. Classify (a) vs (b), find the true root cause, and determine CI impact.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified with a confirmed reproduction and a one-line causal explanation.\n- [ ] Classified: environment/git-version-specific vs genuine main breakage; state whether CI Verified is affected.\n- [ ] If a code/test fix is warranted, it is scoped with file_impact; otherwise an accepted-reason disposition is recorded.\n- [ ] Guidance recorded for the janitor epic on whether full-suite local pre-flight is blocked for all leaves by this cluster.","id":"740d-187c-53a2-4b7d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Pre-existing: 5 tests in test_atomic_completion_close.py fail locally on origin/main (refs/heads/tickets rev-parse exit 128; git 2.55.0)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788474258154670222,"uuid":"518aa08c-6903-4ea4-8f01-087d1bf2136b"}